    "faq": {
      "type": "senseless-faq-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I apply it?",
            "answer": "<p>Start with clean, dry skin and apply a thick, visible layer that sits on the surface rather than being rubbed in. Cover it if your preparation window is longer. Allow time to take effect ahead of your appointment — follow the product guidance and your practitioner. Patch test 24 hours ahead first, and remove before your appointment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before my appointment?",
            "answer": "<p>Allow time to take effect ahead of your appointment; this varies, so follow the product guidance and your practitioner. Don't apply the night before — it's made for the short window before your treatment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does it last?",
            "answer": "<p>It comes down to three things: which strength you've chosen, how well it was applied — a thick layer, covered, left long enough — and how long and demanding the appointment is. Rather than a fixed number of hours, think of it as fading gradually; match the strength to the session so it's working through the part that matters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What size should I get?",
            "answer": "<p>15ml suits a single appointment or a first try; 35ml suits regular bookings or larger areas.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
